  "question": {
    "text": "A tuning fork <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> of unknown frequency produces <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>beats</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;with a fork of known frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>340</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>. When fork <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> is filed, the beat frequency decreases to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>beats</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. What is the frequency of fork <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> ?",
    "image": null
